{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile is the strongest configuration (~0.65 acc), while image-only models are very weak (0.21–0.23 acc for both resnet50 and ViT-L). The critical open question is whether fusing the weak image signal with the strong RNA signal yields any complementary benefit, or whether it merely adds noise. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) is the most direct logical extension of the best RNA-only result, adding the simplest image encoder (resnet50, already characterized) and simplest fusion (concat). It isolates the single question 'does image add value when combined with the best RNA representation?' without confounding changes to encoder, aggregation, or fusion strategy. If it fails to exceed 0.65, it strongly argues against pursuing multimodal configurations and redirects budget to RNA-only refinements; if it succeeds, it justifies further fusion and image-encoder exploration."
}

